Eleft%20for%20Madrid%3C%2Fa%3E%20in%201971.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cfigure%3E%3Cimg%20width%3D%5C%222468%5C%22%20alt%3D%5C%22Old%20photo%20of%20couple%20by%20the%20ocean%5C%22%20src%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fi.insider.com%2F6a4bbe09965805a2c542d20a%3Fformat%3Djpeg%5C%22%20height%3D%5C%221851%5C%22%3E%3Cfigcaption%3EFreddy%20and%20his%20wife%2C%20Adela%2C%20as%20newlyweds%20in%20Stockholm%2C%20Sweden%2C%20in%20the%201970s.%3Cp%3ECourtesy%20of%20the%20author%3C%2Fp%3E%3C%2Ffigcaption%3E%3C%2Ffigure%3E%3Cp%3EDestiny%20took%20him%20to%20Pontevedra%2C%20where%20he%20met%20my%20mom%2C%20a%20local%20dressmaker%20with%20a%20shop%20in%20town.%20They%20married%20in%201975.%20As%20newlyweds%2C%20they%20spent%20time%20in%20Stockholm%20before%20settling%20in%20my%20mother's%20hometown%2C%20where%20my%20brother%20and%20I%20were%20born.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Ch2%20data-toc-id%3D%5C%223f6a69a8-8980-4338-a611-9a5584885bd3%5C%22%3EI%20always%20thought%20of%20my%20dad%20as%20an%20undiscovered%20genius%3C%2Fh2%3E%3Cp%3EHe%20was%20an%20unpublished%20writer%20with%20a%20gift%20for%20explaining%20complex%20ideas%20simply.%20He%20taught%20himself%20classical%20guitar%20and%20piano%2C%20was%20excellent%20at%20maths%2C%20could%20draw%20well%2C%20spoke%20English%2C%20and%20became%20a%20local%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Fmagnus-carlsen-worlds-best-chess-player-losing-motivation-2023-5%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22_blank%5C%22%3Echess%20champion%3C%2Fa%3E%20in%20the%20early%201980s.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EWe%20were%20a%20bit%20of%20an%20eccentric%20family.%20Not%20rich%2C%20but%20culturally%20rich%20and%20surrounded%20by%20our%20beloved%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Fdogs-chernobyl-exclusion-zone-are-genetically-distinct-scientists-say-2023-3%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22_blank%5C%22%3Estray%20dogs%3C%2Fa%3E.%20My%20dad%20loved%20philosophy%20and%20literature%20and%20believed%20the%20mind%20should%20stay%20active.%20As%20a%20teen%2C%20when%20I%20wanted%20a%20computer%2C%20he%20gave%20me%20his%20copy%20of%20Goethe's%20%26quot%3BFaust%26quot%3B%20and%2C%20with%20his%20usual%20wit%2C%20told%20me%2C%20%26quot%3BYour%20brain%20is%20your%20best%20computer!%26quot%3B%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EHis%20brain%20is%20why%20I'm%20writing%20about%20him.%20He's%20now%20one%20of%20millions%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Falzheimers-and-dementia-misconceptions-and-surprising-facts-2018-10%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22_blank%5C%22%3Eliving%20with%20Alzheimer's%3C%2Fa%3E%2C%20a%20form%20of%20dementia%2C%20but%20to%20me%2C%20he's%20my%20one%20in%20a%20million%20%E2%80%94%20my%20brilliant%20dad.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Ch2%20data-toc-id%3D%5C%22382791b9-6423-4f50-b001-3f1bf3071265%5C%22%3EHe%20was%20diagnosed%20at%2071%20with%20Alzheimer's%20and%20is%20now%2077%3C%2Fh2%3E%3Cp%3EFor%20a%20time%2C%20he%20became%20suspicious%20and%20accused%20my%20mother%20of%20stealing%20his%20things.%20She%20felt%20overwhelmed%2C%20and%20we%20tried%20a%20day%20care%20center%2C%20but%20it%20didn't%20work.%20The%20place%20was%20good%2C%20but%20my%20dad%20is%20independent%20and%20stubborn%2C%20so%20he%20wanted%20to%20leave%2C%20questioning%20what%20he%20was%20doing%20among%20%26quot%3Bold%20people%26quot%3B.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cfigure%3E%3Cimg%20width%3D%5C%224032%5C%22%20alt%3D%5C%22Man%20walking%20in%20Pontevedra%5C%22%20src%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fi.insider.com%2F6a4bbe90965805a2c542d20f%3Fformat%3Djpeg%5C%22%20height%3D%5C%223024%5C%22%3E%3Cfigcaption%3ELiving%20in%20a%20small%2C%20walkable%20city%20has%20made%20it%20possible%20for%20the%20author's%20dad%20to%20be%20independent.%3Cp%3ECourtesy%20of%20the%20author%3C%2Fp%3E%3C%2Ffigcaption%3E%3C%2Ffigure%3E%3Cp%3EThe%20big%20turning%20point%20for%20us%20was%20when%20he%20spent%20a%20week%20in%20the%20hospital%20because%20of%20a%20medical%20issue%20unrelated%20to%20Alzheimer's.%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Fwoman-topical-steroid-withdrawal-how-treat-tws-symptoms-2023-7%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22_blank%5C%22%3EBeing%20bed-bound%3C%2Fa%3E%20in%20the%20hospital%20made%20him%20depressed%2C%20and%20it%20was%20difficult%20for%20the%20nurses%20to%20manage%20him.%20They%20regularly%20sedated%20him%20to%20keep%20him%20calm%20and%20to%20stop%20him%20from%20trying%20to%20leave.%20It%20was%20heartbreaking.%20Once%20sedated%2C%20he%20lost%20the%20spirit%20that%20kept%20him%20active.%20That%20experience%20made%20us%20certain%20that%20a%20care%20home%20was%20not%20for%20him.%20We%20feared%20he%20would%20spend%20much%20of%20his%20time%20medicated%20so%20staff%20could%20manage%20him.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Ch2%20data-toc-id%3D%5C%22929772bb-ad3c-4136-96d7-85c9d27678da%5C%22%3EHe%20never%20accepted%20his%20diagnosis%3C%2Fh2%3E%3Cp%3EAt%20every%20neurologist%20appointment%2C%20he%20asked%20why%20he%20was%20there%2C%20calling%20me%20a%20hypochondriac.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EBut%20he's%20a%20fortunate%20man.%20He%20has%20my%20mother.%20Without%20her%2C%20he%20would%20not%20be%20able%20to%20enjoy%20the%20life%20he%20has.%20She%20has%20an%20admirable%20work%20ethic%2C%20and%20by%2011%20a.m.%2C%20she's%20cleaned%20the%20house%2C%20done%20laundry%2C%20shopped%20for%20food%2C%20and%20is%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Fbest-cheap-easy-lunch-ideas-big-family-2023-9%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22_blank%5C%22%3Emaking%20lunch%3C%2Fa%3E.%20Their%20marriage%20is%20far%20from%20perfect%2C%20but%20after%2051%20years%2C%20they%20have%20their%20own%20understanding.%20She's%20the%20practical%20one%20and%20speaks%20in%20Galician%20sayings%20and%20proverbs%20%E2%80%94%20and%20he%20is%20the%20one%20philosophizing%20it%20all.%20When%20they%20argue%20%E2%80%94%20as%20they%20do%20daily%20%E2%80%94%20he%20may%20come%20out%20with%20a%20line%20from%20Nietzsche%20while%20she%20replies%20with%20a%20saying.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cfigure%3E%3Cimg%20width%3D%5C%223648%5C%22%20alt%3D%5C%22Man%20playing%20chess%5C%22%20src%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fi.insider.com%2F6a4bcdd0965805a2c542d2d6%3Fformat%3Djpeg%5C%22%20height%3D%5C%222736%5C%22%3E%3Cfigcaption%3EAlzheimer's%20has%20affected%20the%20author's%20dad's%20short-term%20memory%2C%20but%20many%20of%20the%20skills%20and%20interests%20he%20developed%20earlier%20in%20life%20remain%20intact.%3Cp%3ECourtesy%20of%20the%20author%3C%2Fp%3E%3C%2Ffigcaption%3E%3C%2Ffigure%3E%3Cp%3ELet's%20not%20romanticize%20it%2C%20though.%20He%20can%20be%20exasperating.%20He%20wakes%20regularly%20during%20the%20night%2C%20disrupting%20her%20sleep%2C%20hides%20things%2C%20and%20can%20become%20wary%20and%20distressed%2C%20believing%20his%20IDs%20or%20watch%20have%20been%20taken.%20He%20refuses%20to%20cut%20his%20hair%20and%20wears%20many%20layers%20of%20clothing.%20He%20had%20pneumonia%20in%20his%2020s%20and%20remembers%20it%2C%20so%20he%20wraps%20up%20warm%20all%20year.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EEven%20so%2C%20being%20in%20his%20familiar%20environment%20is%20more%20comforting%20than%20any%20institution%20could%20be.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Ch2%20data-toc-id%3D%5C%22352b2ce9-d27b-482f-9b59-779c1ac30f19%5C%22%3EWe%20want%20him%20to%20have%20independence%3C%2Fh2%3E%3Cp%3ELiving%20in%20a%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Fkids-tried-most-expensive-seafood-galician-percebes-loved-it-2023-8%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22_blank%5C%22%3Esmall%20city%20like%20Pontevedra%3C%2Fa%3E%20has%20helped.%20People%20often%20spot%20him%20walking%20%E2%80%94%20a%20bit%20like%20%26quot%3BWhere's%20Waldo%3F%26quot%3B%2C%20always%20on%20the%20move%20and%20familiar%20to%20many.%20When%20I%20bump%20into%20him%2C%20he%20says%2C%20%26quot%3BI've%20been%20looking%20for%20you%20all%20afternoon!%26quot%3B%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EThis%20independence%20comes%20with%20worries.%20He%20insists%20on%20going%20for%20walks%20even%20when%20told%20not%20to.%20He%20may%20fall%2C%20get%20disoriented%2C%20or%20tell%20caf%C3%A9%20staff%20he%20has%20paid%20when%20he%20hasn't.%20Once%2C%20someone%20brought%20him%20home%20after%20finding%20him%20lost.%20He%20may%20lose%20the%20flip%20phone%2C%20he%20rarely%20answers%2C%20or