ith%20Teri%20Carlyle%2C%2058%2C%20who%20lives%20with%20her%20sister%20and%20father%20in%20Vallejo%2C%20California.%20Carlyle%20said%20the%20%3C%2Fem%3E%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Fhigher-cost-of-living-creating-multigenerational-homes-2026-4%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22_blank%5C%22%3E%3Cem%3Emultigenerational%20living%3C%2Fem%3E%3C%2Fa%3E%3Cem%3E%20arrangement%20has%20worked%20well%20for%20them%20and%20allowed%20the%20family%20to%20cut%20costs.%20This%20interview%20has%20been%20edited%20for%20length%20and%20clarity.%3C%2Fem%3E%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EI've%20had%20an%20amazing%20life.%20I%20knew%20my%20great-grandparents%2C%20so%20I%20know%20what%20it%20looks%20like%20to%20age%20with%20dignity%20and%20grace.%20My%20grandparents%20were%20loving%20and%20supported%20us.%20I've%20traveled%20the%20world%2C%20and%20I'm%20a%20director%20of%20finance%20and%20operations%20at%20a%20nonprofit.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EMy%20parents%20were%20married%20for%2064%20years%20when%20my%20mom%20died.%20My%20mom%20retired%20from%20the%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Fhow-to-set-up-trump-account-1000-dollars-for-child-2026-7%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22_blank%5C%22%3Efederal%20government%3C%2Fa%3E%2C%20while%20my%20dad%20retired%20from%20Sears.%20They%20owned%20a%20motorhome%20and%20traveled%20the%20country%20for%20seven%20months%20out%20of%20the%20year.%20They%20had%20joined%20all%20these%20RV%20clubs.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EBut%20when%20my%20parents%20got%20sick%2C%20they%20came%20to%20live%20with%20me.%3C%2Fp%3E%5Cn%3Caside%3E%5Cn%3Cp%3EAre%20you%20paying%20for%20your%20own%20or%20your%20loved%20one's%20long-term%20care%3F%20Do%20you%20have%20thoughts%20to%20share%20about%20long-term%20care%20in%20the%20US%3F%20To%20share%20your%20story%20with%20a%20reporter%2C%20%3Cstrong%3Eplease%20fill%20out%20this%20%3C%2Fstrong%3E%3Ca%20rel%3D%5C%22noopener%20noreferrer%20nofollow%5C%22%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fdocs.google.com%2Fforms%2Fd%2Fe%2F1FAIpQLSdg4AoiQ9q9GU2sU75z7cCrHvjt0JnM_0Nf34JYn_1DpF3w6A%2Fviewform%3Fusp%3Ddialog%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22_blank%5C%22%3E%3Cstrong%3Equick%20form%3C%2Fstrong%3E%3C%2Fa%3E%3Cstrong%3E.%3C%2Fstrong%3E%3C%2Fp%3E%5Cn%3C%2Faside%3E%5Cn%3Ch2%20data-toc-id%3D%5C%22cd271e06-4b66-4474-a85b-3e3b97b10965%5C%22%3E%3Cstrong%3EMy%20parents'%20health%20started%20to%20decline%3C%2Fstrong%3E%3C%2Fh2%3E%3Cp%3EIn%202021%2C%20my%20father%20had%20a%20stroke.%20Although%20he%20wasn't%20paralyzed%2C%20he%20started%20having%20mobility%20issues%2C%20which%20put%20him%20in%20a%20wheelchair.%20My%20mom%20was%20my%20dad's%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Fbuilt-house-dad-dementia-caregiving-costs-2026-7%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22_blank%5C%22%3Eprimary%20caregiver%3C%2Fa%3E.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EBut%20one%20day%20in%20April%202023%2C%20I%20was%20at%20home%20working%20when%20my%20mom%20passed%20out.%20Little%20did%20we%20know%20that%20she%20had%20a%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2F3-foods-seem-healthy-bad-for-your-heart-cardiologist-2026-6%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22_blank%5C%22%3Eheart%20problem%3C%2Fa%3E.%20She%20was%20healthy%20for%20most%20of%20her%20life%2C%20and%20this%20was%20completely%20out%20of%20the%20blue.%20Her%20legs%20started%20swelling.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EBoth%20of%20them%20needed%20more%20formal%20care%2C%20which%20we%20knew%20we%20had%20to%20pay%20for%20out%20of%20pocket.%20I%20rented%20out%20my%20parents'%20house%20in%202022%2C%20and%20they%20both%20moved%20in%20with%20me.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EIt%20wasn't%20until%20two%20weeks%20before%20she%20died%20that%20we%20found%20out%20how%20severe%20her%20condition%20was.%20She%20was%20in%20the%20ER%20in%20January%202024.%20She%20was%20dying%2C%20and%20the%20doctor%20didn't%20know%20if%20she%20had%20weeks%2C%20months%2C%20or%20years%20left.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3ELuckily%2C%20she%20had%20the%20foresight%20to%20set%20up%20her%20retirement%20so%20that%2C%20when%20she%20died%2C%20my%20dad%20would%20still%20get%20a%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Fboomer-retirement-crisis-millennial-children-financial-support-2026-7%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22_blank%5C%22%3Eretirement%20check%3C%2Fa%3E%20from%20her.%20She%20was%20earning%20around%20%244%2C600%20monthly%2C%20but%20after%20she%20died%2C%20it%20dropped%20to%20%242%2C800.%20We%20had%20to%20find%20a%20way%20to%20make%20up%20this%20difference.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Ch2%20data-toc-id%3D%5C%22fe21c365-9ca9-4a3e-838b-0a7144e968c0%5C%22%3E%3Cstrong%3EIn%20May%202025%2C%20my%20father%20woke%20up%20one%20morning%20and%20wasn't%20able%20to%20use%20any%20words%3C%2Fstrong%3E%3C%2Fh2%3E%3Cp%3EWe%20went%20to%20the%20hospital%20with%20him.%20He%20was%20asleep%20for%20three%20weeks%2C%20and%20we%20didn't%20know%20what%20was%20going%20on.%20My%20sister%20and%20I%20didn't%20leave%20his%20side%20the%20entire%20time.%20Eventually%2C%20he%20started%20coming%20back%20to%20himself.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EI%20now%20have%20a%20caregiver%20who%20comes%20to%20my%20house%20to%20bathe%20and%20feed%20him%2C%20and%20we%20have%20another%20person%20come%20in%20the%20evening%20to%20do%20the%20same.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cfigure%3E%3Cimg%20width%3D%5C%222048%5C%22%20alt%3D%5C%22Teri%20Carlyle%20and%20family%5C%22%20src%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fi.insider.com%2F6a63b6b4548c9c486b310642%3Fformat%3Djpeg%5C%22%20height%3D%5C%221536%5C%22%3E%3Cfigcaption%3ETeri%20Carlyle%20said%20she's%20encouraged%20her%20father%20to%20be%20as%20active%20as%20possible.%3Cp%3ETeri%20Carlyle%3C%2Fp%3E%3C%2Ffigcaption%3E%3C%2Ffigure%3E%3Cp%3EIt's%20a%20blessing%20that%20my%20parents'%20house%20is%20paid%20for.%20My%20sister's%20house%2C%20which%20is%20right%20across%20the%20street%2C%20has%20a%20very%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Fgot-home-cheap-mortgage-payment-stuck-how-getting-out-2026-7%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22_blank%5C%22%3Esmall%20mortgage%3C%2Fa%3E.%20Once%20my%20mom%20passed%2C%20we%20were%20all%20overwhelmed%2C%20and%20I%20told%20my%20sister%20that%20I%20couldn't%20care%20for%20Dad%20by%20myself%2C%20so%20my%20sister%20moved%20in%20with%20me%2C%20too.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EMy%20dad%20is%20able%20to%20be%20here%20with%20us%2C%20and%20there's%20always%20someone%20around.%20We%20know%20we%20will%20never%20put%20him%20in%20a%20facility.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Ch2%20data-toc-id%3D%5C%2234d850c6-6d8a-4389-a36f-4c8facf4b59f%5C%22%3E%3Cstrong%3EWe%20hired%20a%20caregiver%20to%20come%20in%20during%20the%20day%3C%2Fstrong%3E%3C%2Fh2%3E%3Cp%3EWe're%20able%20to%20function%20pretty%20well.%20We%20pay%20%24480%20for%20a%20monthly%20personal%20trainer%20to%20work%20with%20my%20father%20and%20more%20than%20%243%2C000%20a%20month%20for%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Fcaring-for-spouse-working-to-afford-husband-caregiving-costs-2026-7%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22_blank%5C%22%3Ecaregiving%20services%3C%2Fa%3E.%20There%20are%20also%20insurance%20costs.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EWe%20also%20take%20him%20to%20sporting%20events%2C%20concerts%2C%20and%20movies%20every%20now%20and%20then.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EMy%20dad%20gets%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Fcant-retire-grandparents-raising-grandchildren-gas-prices-social-security-costs-2026-3%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22_blank%5C%22%3ESocial%20Security%3C%2Fa%3E%20and%20receives%20my%20mom's%20government%20pension.%20I%20help%20make%20up%20the%20difference.%20My%20brother%20and%20his%20wife%20usually%20buy%20groceries%20and%20other%20things%20to%20help%20out.%20My%20sister%20takes%20care%20of%20some%20tasks%2C%20like%20hiring%20a%20barber%20who%20comes%20to%20the%20house.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Ch2%20data-toc-id%3D%5C%22cf734aa2-bead-451c-adc2-59f9eb46f80e%5C%22%3E%3Cstrong%3EWe're%20trying%20to%20find%20ways%20to%20cut%20costs%3C%2Fstrong%3E%3C%2Fh2%3E%3Cp%3EWe%20want%20to%20sell%20my%20parents'%20motorhome%2C%20but%20it's%20up%20to%20my%20dad%20to%20decide%20whether%20he%20doesn't%20want%20it%20anymore.%20We%20know%20we%20have%20to%20let%20some%20other%20things%20go%2C%20such%20as%20his%20car.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EI'm%20also%20trying%20to%20think%20of%20other%20ways%20to%20increase%20our%20revenue%2C%20such%20as%20renting%20out%20one%20of%20our%20houses%20%E2%80%94%20either%20mine%20or%20my%20sister's.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EOur%20bank%20accounts%20look%20different%20from%20when%20our%20mom%20was%20alive%2C%20but%20we%20also%20don't%20want%20to%20take%20on%20too%20many%20responsibilities%2C%20like%20side%20hustles%2C%20that%20would%20take%20away%20from%20being%20with%20our%20dad.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Ch2%20data-toc-id%3D%5C%2291457b8f-608b-48be-92aa-1908e5e2430e%5C%22%3E%3Cstrong%3EI%20realized%20that%20we%20take%20our%20elders%20for%20granted%3C%2Fstrong%3E%3C%2Fh2%3E%3Cp%3EWe%20don't%20spend%20enough%20time%20with%20our%20elders%20to%20gain%20all%20that%20we%20can%20from%20them.%20Everyone%20needs%20to%20have%20hard%20and%20uncomfortable%20conversations%20while%20everyone%20is%20healthy%2C%20and%20see%20what%20everyone%20wants%20for%20their%20lives.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EYounger%20people%20should%20live%20their%20best%20lives%20because%2C%20one%20day%2C%20they%20might%20have%20to%20come%20home%20and%20take%20care%20of%20their%20parents%2C%20and%20there%20shouldn't%20be%20resentment%20that%20they%20didn't%20get%20to%20do%20anything%20when%20they%20had%20the%20ability%20to.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EPeople%20think%20of%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Fhome-hospice-for-dad-end-of-life-2026-7%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22_blank%5C%22%3Ecaregiving%20as%20a%20burden%3C%2Fa%3E.%20I'm%20living%20through%20a%20beautiful%20nightmare%20because%20it's%20truly%20an%20act%20of%20love%20to%20be%20able%20to%20take%20care%20of%20my%20parents%20and%20let%20them%20see%20that%20I%20love%20them.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cdiv%3ERead%20the%20original%20article%20on%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Fdad-lives-with-daughters-long-term-care-expensive-2026-7%5C%22%3EBusiness%20Insider%3C%2Fa%3E%3C%2Fdiv%3E%22%2C%22published%22%3A1784982421000%2C%22visual%22%3A%22https%3A%2F%2Fi.insider.co